# What must NOT be sent to the Docker daemon when building this image.
#
# The Dockerfile only COPYs requirements.txt, src/ and scripts/, so nothing below would have ended
# up in a layer anyway. This is about the build CONTEXT: without it, every build ships the whole
# directory — including .env and .env.test — to the daemon. Secrets should not make that trip even
# when they do not land in the image, and the rest is just wasted transfer on every rebuild.
#
# The config files are MOUNTED at run time instead (see openai-agent-app/docker-compose.yml), which
# is why excluding them here costs nothing.

# ---- secrets: mounted at run time, never built in ----
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.test.example
service-account.json
*.pem
*.key

# ---- local development clutter ----
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# ---- runtime state and output, which belong to a checkout and not to an image ----
state.json
*.log
downloads/
tmp/

# ---- not needed to run ----
.git/
.gitignore
README.md
deploy/
